=== ROOT CAUSE: the bmv2 liveness path never runs. Evidence chain. ===
1. DeviceConfigurationAndPowerManager.cpp:675 gates the liveness fetch on m_dataPlaneIsBmv2:
     if (m_mode == MININET && m_dataPlaneIsBmv2) p4SwitchState = fetchP4SwitchState();
   fetchP4SwitchState issues  GET http://<proxy>/p4/switch_state  (buildSwitchStateCommand).
2. Proxy access log for the WHOLE life of this fabric: 2 requests to /p4/switch_state,
   and both are mine (curl from ports 60434 and 59126). The kernel issued ZERO,
   against 154 GET /v1.0/... and 94 GET /stats/flow/<n> per switch in the same window.
3. Kernel log contains 0 'cannot read bmv2 liveness from the proxy' warnings, so it did
   not try and fail -- it never tried. => m_dataPlaneIsBmv2 is FALSE at runtime.
4. It is false because of a STARTUP RACE between two threads:
     TopologyAndFlowMonitor::run()  (cpp:2507)
         loadStaticTopologyFromFile()  <- populates m_dpidToSwitchKind at cpp:309
         initializeMappingsFromGraph()
         configureTopologyApiUrls()    <- same all-bmv2 predicate
     DeviceConfigurationAndPowerManager::start() (cpp:124) calls refreshDataPlaneKind(),
     which reads m_dpidToSwitchKind ONCE and caches the answer for the process lifetime
     (header:704 'Cached once by refreshDataPlaneKind()').
   Live timestamps from THIS run's kernel.log:
     00:48:22.689  TopologyAndFlowMonitor.cpp:211 loadStaticTopologyFromFile] Load Static Topology File
     00:48:22.690  DeviceConfigurationAndPowerManager.cpp:121 start] ...Starts Up   <- refreshDataPlaneKind() here
     00:48:22.692  TopologyAndFlowMonitor.cpp:145 configureTopologyApiUrls] All-bmv2 topology: polling ...
   The identical predicate answered TRUE 2 ms after refreshDataPlaneKind() answered FALSE.
   The source comment at cpp:122 asserts the opposite: 'The topology is loaded by
   TopologyAndFlowMonitor before this runs, so the switch-kind index is populated by now.'
5. Consequence: p4LivenessFor() always receives nullopt -> Unknown -> the graph is never
   written. On the P4 plane the twin has NO switch-liveness detection at all.
   Note the proxy HAD the right answer the whole time (probe_ok=false, probe_age_s=1.756,
   last_lldp_age_s=259.4, stream_alive=false), which p4LivenessFor's own policy maps to
   Down (probe fresh < kProbeStaleSeconds=15, LLDP stale > kLldpFreshSeconds=12).

